      <div class="masthead">
        <span class="eyebrow">METHODS &amp; VALIDATION · JAVA'S RICE HARVEST, FROM RADAR</span>
        <h1>Can radar count Java's rice harvest?</h1>
        <p class="standfirst">A stress test of a Sentinel-1 paddy detector over six of Java's largest
        rice regencies, {A.sar_window[0].slice(0, 7)} to {A.sar_window[1].slice(0, 7)}. The instrument
        publishes five failed checks and one diagnosis — that it finds the rice but finds one crop
        where there are two. We factor the shortfall, and find the diagnosis is the wrong way round:
        three-quarters of it is fields never found at all. Then we identify what actually sets the
        detection rate, by taking looks away from a regency that has enough of them.</p>
        <div class="byline">
          <span>openstudy.id</span><span>Data through {A.sar_window[1]}</span>
          <span>{num(A.cells)} cells · {num(A.cycles)} crop cycles</span>
        </div>
      </div>

